    <briefdescription>
<para>STM32 I2C bus — manages the HAL handle and device collection. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>One bus instance per I2C peripheral (I2C1, I2C2, etc.). Devices are created via <ref refid="classStmI2cBus_1a8a8333a7f2c46e1c89da0d80b19e1f79" kindref="member">CreateDevice()</ref> and accessed via <ref refid="classStmI2cBus_1a7d31764b7f52bfd6eaf6249d70231f5d" kindref="member">GetDevice()</ref>.</para>
<para>Transfers are serialized with <ref refid="PlatformMutex_8h_1a3448b54e0a94193058b38d135c1254ef" kindref="member">PlatformMutex</ref> (same contract as StmSpi). Direct HAL probes (IsDeviceReady) must take <ref refid="classStmI2cBus_1aee43d2df39cac7de47bf6f9eba8ef436" kindref="member">LockBus</ref> or risk racing Mem_Read/Master_Transmit on the same handle.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>STM32H7 soft-I2C bring-up contract (parity with <computeroutput>StmSpi</computeroutput>):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Do <bold>not</bold> call <computeroutput>HAL_I2C_IsDeviceReady</computeroutput> from <computeroutput>Initialize</computeroutput> — on STM32H7 it can latch <ref refid="classSoftChipSelectGuard_1acbe56b56922f2d3988c3ecf86208aa4a" kindref="member">ISR.TXIS</ref> while State==READY and poison the next Mem_Read (command byte flushed into TXDR, never on the wire).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Prefer <computeroutput>Master_Transmit</computeroutput> + <computeroutput>Master_Receive</computeroutput> (or WriteRead) over Mem_Read when the slave pointer auto-increments (PCA/PCAL).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>When caller buffers may sit in external FMC SDRAM, stage small RX/TX through D1 AXI scratch before HAL calls (byte loads from that memory class are unreliable on some FMC setups).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Flush sticky TXIS/TXE before a new transfer (<computeroutput>FlushTxdr</computeroutput>). </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
